# Agents per stage, one per line: stage|agent|model|effort|probe
# stage: ralph (`ralph` and sequential `ralph-afk`), worker or reviewer (`ralph-afk --pr`).
# agent: a Ralph agent plugin (`ralph-tui plugins agents`); --pr runs claude and codex only.
# Within a --pr stage, line order is the fallback order; RALPH_AFK_SCHEDULE still decides who may run each hour.
# model: passed as --model. RALPH_<NAME>_MODEL overrides it for the ralph stage, e.g. RALPH_CODEX_MODEL.
# effort: reasoning effort for --pr agents; - means the CLI default. Ralph runs ignore it.
# probe: cheap one-word request, run in /tmp. The agent is usable when the reply contains "pong".
ralph|claude|opus|-|claude -p 'Reply with exactly: pong' --model haiku --effort low
ralph|codex|gpt-6.2-sol|-|codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --ephemeral -s read-only -m gpt-6-luna -c 'model_reasoning_effort="low"' 'Reply with exactly: pong'
worker|claude|sonnet|high|claude -p 'Reply with exactly: pong' --model haiku --effort low
worker|codex|gpt-6.2-sol|medium|codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --ephemeral -s read-only -m gpt-6-luna -c 'model_reasoning_effort="low"' 'Reply with exactly: pong'
reviewer|claude|opus|high|claude -p 'Reply with exactly: pong' --model haiku --effort low
